<h2 id="sources">Sources and method</h2><p>Dodds et al. (2014), <em>Grip Strength across the Life Course</em>, is the primary source for the distinction between age-related handgrip-force norms and timed hanging. The personal-goal examples on this page are arithmetic and editorial milestones, not research-derived training prescriptions.</p><p>Read our <a href="/editorial-standards/">editorial standards</a> for how we distinguish research, interpretation and equipment advice.</p>
